    <p>Passenger-car starter batteries are usually 12V; heavy-duty applications can also use 6V. Confirm the system voltage of the target vehicle.</p>

    <h2>Capacity (Ah)</h2>
    <p>Capacity describes the battery&rsquo;s energy content over a defined discharge test. It must be read with the standard because the same physical size can carry different ratings across families.</p>

    <h2>CCA</h2>
    <p>Cold cranking amps indicate starting performance at low temperature. CCA values are test-method dependent and must carry a reference basis — for example JIS (-15&deg;C) or EN (-18&deg;C). Always confirm final CCA with the manufacturer before ordering.</p>

    <h2>Dimensions, terminal and polarity</h2>
    <p>Fix length &times; width &times; height in millimetres, terminal type and polarity. If a field is not yet known, mark it &ldquo;confirm on inquiry&rdquo; rather than guessing.</p>

    <h2>Reference models</h2>
    <div class="model-list">
      {batteryModels.map((model) => <ModelCard model={model} />)}
    </div>
    <p>Specifications above are for reference; confirm final values with the manufacturer. <a href="/tools/battery-finder/">Use the battery finder &rarr;</a></p>

    <h2>Dingwei Battery view</h2>
    <p>{RELATIONSHIP} {MANUFACTURER.name} manufactures to JIS, DIN, BCI, AS and SA standards.</p>
    <p><a href="/oem/">Start an OEM program &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <CTASection title="Finalize your battery specification" />
</ArticleLayout>

